### Australian Commission on Safety and Quality in Health Care (ACSQHC) Standards

#### Incident Management and Open Disclosure
Health services must have systems in place for managing patient safety incidents, including:
**Reporting**: Documenting all incidents.
**Reviewing**: Regularly reviewing incident data to identify trends and areas for improvement.
**Open Disclosure**: Communicating with patients and their families about incidents and the steps taken to prevent recurrence [1](https://www.safetyandquality.gov.au/our-work/indicators-measurement-and-reporting) [2](https://www.safetyandquality.gov.au/standards/nsqhs-standards).

These requirements ensure comprehensive management of patient safety incidents, promoting transparency and continuous improvement in healthcare.

[1](https://www.safetyandquality.gov.au/our-work/indicators-measurement-and-reporting): [ACSQHC - Incident Management and Open Disclosure](https://www.safetyandquality.gov.au/)
[2](https://www.safetyandquality.gov.au/standards/nsqhs-standards): SA Health - Clinical Incident Management and Open Disclosure


